{"en": "1530822677", "title": "Configuration du mappage analyses/types d'échantillons pour le déploiement à Madagascar", "adf": {"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"localId": "84604340bf73"}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Dépôt :", "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " "}, {"type": "text", "text": "DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2", "marks": [{"type": "link", "attrs": {"href": "https://github.com/DIGI-UW/OpenELIS-Global-2"}}]}, {"type": "text", "text": ", branche "}, {"type": "text", "text": "madagascar", "marks": [{"type": "code"}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"localId": "669ccf60f6b8"}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Ce domaine définit les types d'échantillons valides pour chaque analyse (par exemple, la glycémie peut être réalisée sur sérum, plasma ou sang total). C'est l'équivalent autonome de la colonne "}, {"type": "text", "text": "sampleType", "marks": [{"type": "code"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " intégrée au CSV "}, {"type": "text", "text": "tests", "marks": [{"type": "code"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " : mêmes données sous-jacentes, point d'entrée différent."}]}, {"type": "table", "attrs": {"layout": "default", "width": 760.0, "localId": "30a86773-f9be-4de0-9ce8-b5bfa7bef5ef"}, "content": [{"type": "tableRow", "attrs": {"localId": "00a1906b-997b-40ad-933a-17f70a4e2bce"}, "content": [{"type": "tableHeader", "attrs": {"colspan": 1, "rowspan": 1, "localId": "a3344d34-20e7-4f22-abbb-a1d051550a6c"}, "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"localId": "bc682a72d30c"}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Domaine"}]}]}, {"type": "tableHeader", "attrs": {"colspan": 1, "rowspan": 1, "localId": "f714b8d8-f5d8-4d2a-9ff2-7a85cc7f98d0"}, "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "attrs": {"localId": "939b7de41392"}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Objectif"}]}]}, {"type": "tableHeader", "attrs": {"colspan": 1, "rowspan": 1, "localId": "3eb7eb64-d1cf-4931-bc8c-4ffc30deaccd"}, "content": [{"type": "paragrap